{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And the sense: \"These are the generations of Jacob\" — these are the events that happened to him, and the occurrences that came upon him, from the root-meaning of \"what a day may give birth to\" (Proverbs 27:1)." "<b>And he was a lad with the sons of Bilhah and with the sons of Zilpah.</b> Because he was young, the sons of the handmaids made him serve them, for if he had served his brothers the sons of the mistress, it would not have been a bad thing. And this is \"their evil report.\" And the sense of \"a limb from the living\" is midrashic, for Scripture did not mention of his brothers anyone except the sons of the handmaids."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:13.458100324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}